M(T, 'Hearing aids work by', 'amplifying sound', ['bypassing the cochlea', 'replacing the auditory nerve', 'removing earwax'], 'They suit people with some working hair cells.')
M(T, 'Myopia (short-sightedness) is corrected with', 'a concave (diverging) lens', ['a convex lens', 'a cochlear implant', 'a hearing aid'], 'The image forms in front of the retina; a diverging lens moves it back.')
